{"cluster_id": "C-1587", "topic": "fold barrier treats a create-precommit as non-activating until its manifest body", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B001-074", "B002-017", "B010-079"], "canonical_claim": "The fold barrier treats a create-precommit as non-activating until its manifest body is present; once present, manifest expansion contributes the activating +1 blob edges.; GC must not advance a fold cursor past a live precommit whose manifest body is absent or fails `RefMatchesBody` or `ManifestNamespaceMatches` validation.; A live owner newly entering the fold requires a valid manifest body, an inherited-owner removal requires that body to emit `-1`, a move preserving the same `ManifestRef` emits no delta, and a missing required manifest aborts the entire GC attempt.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/03-writer-protocol.md#L434-L451", "docs/superpowers/cas/04-gc-protocol.md#fold", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#fold-algorithm"]}
